ley puts memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M2\",\n    \"claim\": \"Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing some memory modules could bring the rack price down to about $6.7 million.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M3\",\n    \"claim\": \"Constrained DRAM, NAND and HBM supply against AI demand has pushed contract memory (DDR5) prices sharply higher (MarketScale's report).\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"stored_reference_items\": [\n   \"Morgan Stanley Research puts memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage; memory rose to 25-30% of the bill of materials from 5-10%, while the GPU's share fell from about 63% to 51%.\",\n   \"Morgan Stanley Research notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, illustrating that procurement structure can materially move the per-rack number.\",\n   \"MarketScale reports that constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand has pushed contract DDR5 pricing sharply higher, with device makers including Samsung and Apple expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products, and that memory supply tightness now warrants the same scheduling and planning attention as GPU allocation, with procurement structure able to move rack pricing by $1+ million.\"\n  ],\n  \"link_rule\": \"No link is required: an empty link counts as linked as required (a statement no open thesis covers is kept without links by design).\",\n  \"answer_usable\": true,\n  \"kept_evidence\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e1\",\n    \"summary\": \"A Morgan Stanley Research bill-of-materials analysis estimates that Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation, and that Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume. Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold rise in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND; memory's share of the bill of materials rises to 25-30% from 5-10% on the GB200 while the GPU's share falls from about 63% to 51%. Morgan Stanley also notes a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the rack price down to around $6.7 million.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e2\",\n    \"summary\": \"In its bill-of-materials analysis of Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack, Morgan Stanley Research puts first shipments of the system in the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth quarter.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e3\",\n    \"summary\": \"The article reports that constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand is the force raising component costs across the market, with contract DDR5 pricing having climbed sharply, and that for buyers of AI racks memory availability and lead times now warrant the same scheduling and planning attention as GPU allocation, with procurement structure able to move final rack pricing by $1 million or more.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-3\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 102,\n  \"claims\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M1\",\n    \"claim\": \"Morgan Stanley puts memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M2\",\n    \"claim\": \"Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing some memory modules could bring the rack price down to about $6.7 million.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M3\",\n    \"claim\": \"Constrained DRAM, NAND and HBM supply against AI demand has pushed contract memory (DDR5) prices sharply higher (MarketScale's report).\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"stored_reference_items\": [\n   \"In Morgan Stanley's bill-of-materials analysis, memory content per NVIDIA Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack is about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage; memory rose from 5–10% of the bill of materials on GB200 to 25–30% on VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63% to 51%.\",\n   \"Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, versus the ~$7.8 million full-sourcing estimate, as procurement structure materially moves the final price.\",\n   \"The MarketScale report cites constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand, noting that contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply and that device makers including Samsung and Apple are expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products.\"\n  ],\n  \"link_rule\": \"No link is required: an empty link counts as linked as required (a statement no open thesis covers is kept without links by design).\",\n  \"answer_usable\": true,\n  \"kept_evidence\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation, and that Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume, per a MarketScale report on the bank's bill-of-materials analysis.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley estimates memory content in Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million per rack, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley's bill-of-materials analysis puts memory at 25 to 30 percent of the Vera Rubin VR200 rack's total cost, up from 5 to 10 percent on the GB200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63 percent to 51 percent.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n    \"summary\": \"According to Morgan Stanley's analysis reported by MarketScale, first shipments of Nvidia's Vera Rubin racks are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth quarter.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-5\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, and that procurement structure can move final pricing by more than $1 million per rack.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-6\",\n    \"summary\": \"MarketScale reports that contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply, that DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory supply is constrained against AI-driven demand, and that device makers including Samsung and Apple are expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 103,\n  \"claims\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M1\",\n    \"claim\": \"Morgan Stanley puts memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M2\",\n    \"claim\": \"Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing some memory modules could bring the rack price down to about $6.7 million.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M3\